Feature: slice-4 / admin-orgs-list (+ admin-org-detail, shipped together)
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-4-cont
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.2 (admin orgs list + detail)

What was built
==============
- /admin/orgs route + OrgsList client component:
    • Calls identityClient.adminListOrganizations({pageSize: 25, ...}).
    • Hand-rolled responsive HTML table with 6 columns: legal_name,
      type, status (active/blocked badge with magma/Ember colour),
      therapists_count, last_session_at (Intl.DateTimeFormat per
      locale), actions (Open → /admin/orgs/[id]).
    • Search input with 300ms debounce → passes `search` to the
      backend (PG ILIKE on legal_name).
    • Cursor-based pagination via next_page_token. Page-stack
      tracks history so the "Previous page" button works (the proto
      doesn't expose backward cursors, so we walk the stack).
    • Tolerant enum handling: Connect-Web JSON wire format ships
      OrganizationType as proto NAMES, but proto-es types it as the
      numeric enum. Cast through unknown and compare against both
      shapes — same trick that worked for UserRole in the
      AdminGuard (Slice 4 feature 1).
- /admin/orgs/[id] route + OrgDetail client component:
    • Calls identityClient.adminGetOrganization → OrganizationDetails
      (organization + therapists + recent_audit, 20 entries cap from
      backend).
    • Three-card layout: Details (id, NIP, VAT-EU, address,
      created_at), Therapists list, Recent activity audit panel
      with Ember-left-border entries showing action / actor email /
      timestamp / reason.
    • Loading / not-found / error states. Back-to-list link in the
      header.

New i18n keys (messages/{pl,en}.json):
  admin.orgs.* — title, subhead, searchPlaceholder, loading,
                 empty, error, retry, prev, next, view, columns.*,
                 status.{active,blocked}, typeLabel.*, noLastActivity
  admin.orgDetail.* — title via metaTitle, loading, notFound,
                      backToList, sectionDetails / Therapists /
                      Audit, noTherapists, noAudit

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table now includes:
     /[locale]/admin/orgs       ● SSG (×2 locales)
     /[locale]/admin/orgs/[id]  ƒ Dynamic

2. HTTP smoke: all 4 URL shapes (PL + EN × list + detail) return
   200. The page renders the AdminGuard's "sign-in required"
   panel for anonymous puppeteer sessions — which proves the
   layout's guard is doing its job AND the routes are reachable.

3. Puppeteer screenshots:
     orgs-list-gate-pl-full.png   — Polish sign-in card on
       /admin/orgs. Auth flow is correct: guard fires before
       any RPC, so no console errors from a failed
       adminListOrganizations call without a token.
     orgs-list-gate-en-full.png   — same in English.
     orgs-detail-gate-pl-full.png — same gate on the dynamic
       detail route, proving the route matcher binds [id].

4. preview_console_logs(error) returns "No console logs" — the
   guard's getMyProfile catch swallows the unauthed RPC failure
   silently and sets status="forbidden"/"signed-out".

Compliance with docs/18 §8.2
============================
- ✓ Orgs list: "filterable table; columns: org name, plan,
  status, therapists count, tokens used / limit, last activity".
  Implemented: legal_name, type (substituting for "plan" — plan
  tier lives on subscriptions, not org; we'll surface it in the
  detail page via the AdminListOrganizations summary once the
  proto adds it), status, therapists_count, last_session_at.
  "tokens used / limit" deferred — needs a separate billing-svc
  summary RPC we don't have yet.
- ✓ Org detail: usage chart deferred (no sessions-per-day RPC
  in the proto), therapist list + audit log surfaced.
- ✓ Click row → detail page: implemented.
- ✓ Single-role guard re-enforces SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN — the
  AdminGuardAndShell layout from feature 1 wraps everything
  under /admin.

Known gaps (deferred)
=====================
- "Plan tier" column on the list view — backend's
  OrganizationSummary doesn't expose it yet; the detail page's
  /admin/orgs/[id] could surface it via a follow-on call to
  billing-svc.GetSubscription but that's not implemented yet.
- Usage chart on detail — proto needs a sessions-per-day RPC.
- Live screenshot of the populated table requires an
  authenticated SUPERWIZOR_ADMIN session with seeded org rows
  (same constraint as all backend-dependent features in Slices
  3, 4, 5). The Slice 3 feature 8 Playwright intercept pattern
  is the path to evidence it when needed.

